# Continental Control Systems WattNode WNC.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Continental Control Systems WattNode WNC — 3-Phase Energy Meter (Modbus RTU/TCP)
# | 
# | Source: continental-wattnode-wnc-modbus-manual.pdf (pp. 32-50)
# | Models: WNC-3Y-208-MB, WNC-3Y-400-MB, WNC-3Y-480-MB, WNC-3Y-600-MB,
# | WNC-3D-240-MB, WNC-3D-400-MB, WNC-3D-480-MB
# | Protocol: Modbus RTU or TCP; FC03/FC04 read (interchangeable), FC06/FC16 write
# | Baud: 9600 or 19200 (DIP switch); overridable via register 1652
# | Register numbering: source uses 1-based numbers; TOML addresses are 0-based (source - 1).
# | 32-bit values: low 16 bits at the listed address, high 16 bits at address+1 (little-endian words).
# | Floating point: IEEE 754 f32, low word first.
# | Integer energy (s32): units of 0.1 kWh, 0.1 kVARh, or 0.1 kVAh.
# | Integer power (s16): units of PowerIntScale watts (reg 1608, default auto).
# | Integer voltage (s16): units of 0.1 V.
# | Integer current (s16): scaled by CtAmps/CurrentIntScale.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Continental Control Systems
@model=WattNode WNC
@description=3-phase energy meter, Modbus RTU/TCP. FC03/04 read, FC06/16 write. Basic FP (f32): energy kWh at 1000-1006, power W at 1008-1014, voltage V at 1016-1030, freq at 1032. Advanced FP: per-phase energy+reactive+apparent at 1100-1136, PF at 1138-1144, reactive/apparent power at 1146-1160, current A at 1162-1166, demand at 1168-1180. Integer equivalents (s32 energy, s16 power/volt/current) at 1200-1220 (basic) and 1300-1361 (advanced). Config at 1600-1622. Comms at 1650-1655. Diagnostics at 1700-1722.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/continental-wattnode-wnc.toml; Source: continental-wattnode-wnc-modbus-manual.pdf (pp. 32-50). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
